{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ</b> (My strength and the praise of Yah). Ibn Ezra explained that the word עָזִּי is distributive: <b>עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת</b> — עָזִּי יָהּ. The meaning is: he gave thanks that His might and His power, which one sings of, is HaShem, and He was my salvation. <b>זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ</b> (This is my El and I will beautify Him) — I will cause Him to dwell in a habitation. <b>אֱלֹהֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ</b> (The Elohim of my father and I will exalt Him) — that I will recount His mighty deeds. And this is certainly the plain sense of Scripture. But he did not mention the full Name; he mentioned only two letters of it. And the way of Moses our teacher throughout the entire Torah is to mention the great Name in its entirety, as He said to him: 'This is My name forever and this is My remembrance for all generations' (Exodus 3:15). And the Sages already expounded (Tanhuma, end of parashat Ki Tetzei) on the verse 'For a hand upon the throne of Yah' (Exodus 17:16): the Holy One, blessed be He, swore that the throne is not whole and the Name is not complete until the seed of Amalek is blotted out.\n\nAnd by way of truth: because the salvation at the sea was entirely through the Angel of Elohim — this is what is written about him, 'For My name is within him' (Exodus 23:21), and as He said, 'And Israel saw the great hand' (Exodus 14:31) — for 'the hand' alludes to the attribute of Judgment, which is the great and avenging hand, and it is what cleaves the sea, as the Prophet explained: 'Awake, awake, put on strength' (Isaiah 51:9), 'Are you not she who hacks apart the sea, the waters of the great deep?' (Isaiah 51:10), and as I wrote above (see above on 14:31). Therefore he said that His might and His praise is this Name, which is in יָהּ — 'For in Yah, YHWH, is an everlasting rock' (Isaiah 26:4). And thus he explained: 'What ails you, O sea, that you flee?' (Psalms 114:5) — 'Before the Eloah of Jacob' (Psalms 114:7). And so they said in the Mekhilta (Beshallah 3): the Shekhinah went down into the sea with them, as it is written, 'And the Angel of Elohim moved' (Exodus 14:19). And in Shemot Rabbah (30:1) he said: there is no עֹז (might) except Judgment, as it is written, 'And the king's might loves justice' (Psalms 99:4).\n\n<b>זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ</b> — and I will raise Him up to the habitation of the Most High. <b>אֱלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי</b> — who appeared to them as El Shaddai, and now I will exalt Him with the full Name, for from now on <b>HaShem is a man of war</b> and YHWH is <b>His name</b>, in the sense of 'Now I will raise myself up, now I will lift myself up' (Isaiah 33:10). And it is possible that this alludes to seven sefirot in wisdom, like 'This is My name forever and this is My remembrance' (Exodus 3:15). And in the Mekhilta (Beshallah 3): <b>אֵלִי</b> — with me He conducted with the attribute of Mercy, and with my fathers with the attribute of Judgment. And whence do we know that אֵלִי means only the attribute of Mercy? As it is written, 'My El, my El, why have You forsaken me?' (Psalms 22:2), 'El, please heal her, please' (Numbers 12:13), 'El is YHWH and He has illumined us' (Psalms 118:27). And if so, he says <b>זֶה אֵלִי</b> — for with me He is 'El' in this, for He is exalted together with Mercy to be merciful in His judgment."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:17:09.392930413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}